---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
import { LINKS } from '../config'
---

<Base
  title="Hermes Agent"
  description="Hermes is the agent that walks an ICM folder structure. What it is, why it pairs with folders, and where the full setup guide lives."
  path="/hermes"
>
  <section>
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <span class="badge">Hermes Agent</span>
      <h1>The agent that walks the folders</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        ICM gives you the structure. Hermes is what moves through it.
      </p>

      <h2>Why they go together</h2>
      <p>
        A folder structure on its own is just tidy. It becomes useful the moment
        something reads it and acts. Hermes runs on your machine, reads the
        folder you point it at, and does the job that folder describes.
      </p>
      <p>
        It also connects out: Discord, Telegram, email, and scheduled jobs that
        run without you sitting there. So the same folders that tell it how you
        write can also be the thing that sends you a summary every morning.
      </p>

      <div class="callout">
        <p>
          <strong>The full setup guide lives here:</strong>
          <a href={LINKS.hermesGuide}>profiles.agentsasfolders.ai</a>. Keys,
          logins, providers, tools, the whole configuration walkthrough. It is
          the deep reference and it stays current.
        </p>
      </div>

      <h2>What you need before you start</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Hermes installed and running.</li>
        <li>
          A folder structure worth pointing it at. That is
          <a href="/start">the 3 folder start</a>.
        </li>
        <li>One real file inside 1 of those folders. Not a prompt. A note.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>The part people miss</h2>
      <p>
        You do not paste your context in. You do not build a giant instruction
        block. You put a file in a folder and you point the agent at the folder.
        The folder does the explaining.
      </p>

      <div class="btn-row">
        <a class="btn" href={LINKS.hermesGuide}>Open the setup guide</a>
        <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/start">Build the folders first</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
